orld peace the  entry for scp-6001 on the scp archive  opens with an email addressed to us from  a member of foundation personnel called  david caspian that reads hey sorry i  know it's late but i just had to share  this with someone there is no one in the  world i'd rather share it with than you  i just had the most incredible day then  as the article continues there are  numerous format changes from the  standard scp foundation entries that  we're familiar with in particular the  type of terminology is vastly altered  from what we'd be familiar with the term  scp is now phenom special containment  procedures have been replaced with modis  imprimus takes the place of description  and even the name of the organization is  different the compendium phenomic  inquiry this appears to be a version of  the scp foundation that exists in some  kind of parallel universe or alternate  timeline to the foundation that we know  phenom 6001 itself is a tiny microscopic  singularity uncovered in the tokyo of  this other universe's japan this  singularity is linked to another version  of tokyo from another universe which is  referred to as a6k this universe a6k is  described by the compendium as being  similar to their own reality in almost  every superficial and surface level way  it looks the same contains the same  people the same places and even the same  anomalies but that is where the  similarities end the a6k universe  diverges from this baseline by having a  general lack of cooperation among its  inhabitants scientific repression along  with heightened paranoia aggression and  levels of violence sound familiar it  should because a6k's main scientific  institution is a group known as the scp  foundation  that's right a6k is the foundation's  reality the foundation is aware of what  it refers to as scp-6001  but because of the tiny size of the  singularity that links their world with  that of the compendium none of their  personnel are able to travel through to  that reality the compendium states that  it is considering unifying with the  foundation striking up an alliance  between universes however they both have  dramatically different approaches which  would likely get in the way of that the  scp foundation has always been shrouded  in secrecy never revealing anything to  the public often eliminating or memory  wiping anyone who witnesses an anomaly  just to keep everything under wraps  meanwhile in their universe the cpi has  willingly made its documents and  anomalous information available to  anyone that asks for it in the  foundation's reality the world they were  linked to via scp-6001 was seemingly  first discovered when david caspian the  personnel member we mentioned earlier  hunched over the spot where the  singularity was located for almost five  minutes he had been doing this for a  number of weeks since the foundation's  instruments first detected the existence  of the tiny hole connecting a6k with  another dimension david's focus had been  so fixated on that spot where  scp-6001 was that it wasn't until he got  back up that he realized he was in a  completely different universe he  described tall rounded skyscrapers  unlike the tokyo of the foundation's  world gigantic ivy growing up the  buildings with leaves the size of cars  the clouds above had been replaced with  the clearest blue sky and clean fresh  air took the place of the stale polluted  environment david had just left a nearby  cat was perched on the same rooftop as  david watching strange seed-shaped glass  constructs floating on the horizon  filled with lush green innards the cat  had a coat of spotted orange white and  browned underneath an actual coat a  violet blazer complete with a white bow  under the collar and a black brooch  pinned to it the shape of an eye inside  a globe it even wore a pair of  spectacles the cat primrose greeted  david by name and introduced herself the  pair sharing a brief joke about stepping  through the looking glass both of them  were doctors in fact david was the  foundation's head of alt-dimensional  research when he asked pimrose how he'd  arrived on her side of scp-6001  she responded by asking if he had heard  of something called cross-dimensional  test sampling of course david was more  than familiar with it not only was it a  standard procedure for the scp  foundation but one that he himself had  written the procedure involved bringing  an isolated part of another reality to a  safe environment within one's own for  testing purposes this is exactly what  the compendium had done to bring david  to their universe according to primrose  the compendium had many similar  procedures to the foundation causing  david to ask why if this was the case he  wasn't being scanned or checked for  contaminants and pathogens or paralyzed  to prevent kinatographic mimetics  primrose responded by simply asking if  he had eaten breakfast and seemingly  inviting him to paris primrose then sat  with david on an armchair on the tokyo  rooftop and spoke an address to it the  next moment she and david were  transported to paris in a courtyard  filled with similar chairs that other  people and animals were using to  teleport primrose referred to them as  the everywhere chair a form of public  transport david remarked that there was  something similar in the a6k universe  referring to scp-1609  which was destroyed by the global occult  coalition the cat responded by saying  that david would find many similarities  between their universes and mentioned  that she was the department head of  trans-dimensional development and  discovery for the cpi but then primrose  declared she no longer wanted to discuss  work as she was already off the clock  despite it only being the early hours of  the morning when david questioned this  primrose replied the wonders of  automation david more hands make less  work and we have a lot of hands besides  i have something more important lined up  for today she then ordered uh royier  from a holographic menu and david  ordered the same remarking when in rome  or paris or a parallel reality with  talking cats he'd do as the romans david  then asked primrose about the compendium  learning that it was the primary  scientific institute but it lacked the  employees of the scp foundation primrose  and her fellow researchers were under no  obligation to work for the cpi but  rather were able to choose to work with  them out of their own curiosity or  interest the compendium was also  responsible for running the governments  economies and law enforcement of the  entire world with primrose likening the  organization to benevolent dictators  david then expressed surprise that  people didn't resist the compendium  taking control of the world to which his  feline counterpart replied goodness no  governments certainly corporations  absolutely the people though imagine a  foreign power suddenly swooping in and  saying hey there so we're in charge now  here's universal healthcare living wages  housing infrastructure and total liberty  from anyone but us and literally all we  ask you is to respect basic human rights  that's it we provide the rest tax-free  this also includes ethically replicated  barbecue instant global transport and  adorable talking animals also the cure  to cancer can you really think of anyone  so wedded to the existing power  structures that they just say no to all  that it is easy to see why people would  so willingly accept something so  universally beneficial by the time the  compendium had gone public they already  had been working with world governments  in the shadows much like the scp  foundation at first the public response  had been rough but all it took was a few  years of human life on earth improving  to help the naysayers change their tune  partway through their meal david and  primrose discussed the compendium  further she revealed that something  called pact 15 was currently in the  process of being rolled out worldwide  pact stood for phenom application and or  combination technology phenoms being the  cpi term for an scp or anomaly the  initiative had come about after the  compendium studied an australian talking  spider or  scp-1470 as david knew it the goal of  pax was to find a use for phenoms that  would not only be beneficial to the  people of their universe but would also  benefit the phenoms themselves these  creatures objects or entities were all  given the freedom to choose whether or  not they complied and those that did  would find their existence to be bliss  david was given a tour of primrose's  world encountering all manner of  familiar scps that had been repurposed  and allowed to live their best possible  lives alongside human beings living in  uninterrupted peace for example dr kleff  seemingly pulled off the impossible by  finally curing 682 of its aggression  shortly after finding a whole nest of  the creatures 682 species dubbed the  emortagons have since both proliferated  and really mellowed out with the og-682  stating that it no longer finds humans  disgusting another nightmarish anomaly  from david's universe  scp-173 the sculpture has found a new  lease on life in this world too it lives  in a museum adored by everyone who sees  it and it uses a mere second of being  unseen every night to reshape itself  into a new beautiful construction turns  out a lot of its aggression merely came  from being confined as a piece of art it  wanted to be looked at and loved not  locked away and feared meanwhile however  the various groups that formed the  compendium phenomic inquiry were casting  their votes on what would be done about  the residents of dimension a6k  what would they do about the foundation  some among the compendium saw the people  of their neighboring universe as  prisoners needing liberation groups  known as the wanderers and the charity  hoped to save universe a6k to heal a  world in need of their help after all  this universe had a means to cure  diseases and famines and ultimately  achieve total peace and wanted to share  their gifts with the foundation's world  however one by one opposing votes were  cast other groups like the synthetic  assembly looked to how a6k treated  machines like slaves refusing them of  their own free agency  another known as the partnership of  three argued that a6k held no value  their natural resources deplete at a  staggering rate the labor force is  sickly and untrained their cultural  dissimilarities are  well laughable we have everything they  have and what little uniqueness they  bring to market so to speak isn't worth  its counter space they wouldn't even  make a good tourist trap but kind of  morbid sob would want to visit these  wonders of theirs it's all tombs and  constructs of war or crumbling  architecture where people would fight  each other to the death for spot and who  defaces a perfectly good mountain like  that with a bunch of dead people's faces  some of the compendium claimed that the  people of universe a6k had to learn to  overcome their own adversities rather  than the easy option for their  universe's people to come in to fix  everything others simply claimed that  a6k was just irredeemable it's people  not to be trusted finally the vote was  settled the compendium would deny help  to the foundation and its universe and  would seal  scp-6001 just enough to keep them out  but they would watch over a 6k and the  day when the people of that universe  were ready to come and ask for the  compendium's help the day they were  ready to finally know world peace they  would be welcomed with open arms  needless to say that day hasn't arrived  yet we just really  really hope it does sometime soon one  person however did get a happy ending in  this story none other than david himself  who now works blissfully in a bar in  alternate osaka we'd love to be happy  for him but frankly we're a little too  jealous now go check out scp-001 when  day breaks and scp-001 oroboro cycle the  full story compilation for more  alternate universe craziness

